      "content": "It is completely understandable that you feel exhausted when the framework of your life has vanished; it's a monumental shift. Even when the old structure is gone, the capacity to create something new, however small, still exists within you. Instead of focusing on the vastness of what's missing, perhaps you could focus on just getting through the next hour, one small, manageable moment at a time. Reaching out to someone who can listen without judgment can provide a little bit of grounding in this overwhelming space.",
      "source": "target",
