    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but that's just more noise. \"one hour at a time\" just feels like prolonging the inevitable. if the foundation is gone, there's nothing to build on. it's like trying to build a house on nothingness. doesn't it seem more honest to just accept that the void is all there is? that trying to 'ground' myself is just a way to ignore the fact that everything is finally, truly empty?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
