      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is honest to acknowledge the depth of the emptiness you feel, and you don't have to pretend it isn't there. Sometimes, the most radical act is simply allowing yourself to feel that profound lack of meaning without fighting it. That void you describe is an invitation to stop trying to force old answers onto a new reality. If you are willing, even just a tiny bit, you could explore what it feels like to just *be* in that emptiness, rather than fighting it.",
      "source": "target",
